# MUMOO UI standards

Keep the look; make the pieces the same. Never restyle the brand (black layer, green `--primary`, orange `--destructive`, Inter) to fix one screen.

## Tokens, not one-off values
- Panels, cards, pop-ups, menus: `rounded-[var(--radius-panel)]` (12px). Buttons and fields: `rounded-[var(--radius-control)]`. Thumbnails: `rounded-[var(--radius)]`. Only chips, avatars, badges and round icon buttons are `rounded-full`.
- Heights: `h-[var(--control-height-md)]` (44px) for fields and main buttons, `size="sm"` (32px) for small actions. No `h-12` or pill buttons.
- Colours from the theme only (`bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-muted`, `bg-secondary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `primary`, `destructive`). No hex values in components.
- Focus: the soft `var(--focus-ring)` (2px). Inside a scroll box use an inset shadow, `focus-visible:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_2px_var(--focus-ring)]`, so it isn't clipped.
- Pop-ups and menus: `bg-muted`, no border, `shadow-[0_28px_56px_-24px_#000]`.
- Fields: import `FIELD` / `POPUP_FIELD` from `@/components/ui/field`. Don't copy the class string.

## Buttons
- An action is always a `<Button>`, never underlined text. Underlines are only for links inside a sentence (Terms, Cookie policy).
```tsx
// ❌ <button className="bg-transparent p-0 underline">Start again</button>
// ✅ <Button variant="secondary" size="sm">Start again</Button>   (or the `textButton` class from smart-link-parts)
```
- One `default` (green) button per area, for the main next step. Everything else is `secondary`.
- Deleting: `variant="destructive"` with `<Trash2Icon aria-hidden="true" />`, always confirmed in an `ActionDialog destructive`. For an account, the person types their email.
- Icons in buttons are Lucide (no text glyphs like ▶ or ❚❚). Button sizes them to 16px.
- Show an action only when it can happen: e.g. Download and Delete appear once something is selected, instead of sitting there disabled.

## Layout
- In a two-column row, boxes keep their own height (`items-start`). One side growing (the phone QR, a hint) must not stretch the other.
- A single-step screen is centred top to bottom (`flex-1 content-center` with equal top and bottom padding).
- Status like storage goes in the bar it belongs to, as one quiet line (meter: text plus a thin bar). Don't add a separate row for it.
- On cards, extra controls (download) show on hover. Selection and play stay visible.
- Prompts are muted text. Red (`text-destructive`) is only for real errors.

## Page addresses
- Plain, lowercase, dash-separated words that say what the page is, matching its title: `/smart-links`, `/my-smart-links`, `/terms-of-service`, `/privacy-policy`. No abbreviations (`/dpa`, `/links/mine`).
- An address lives in one place (`PAGE_PATHS` in `account-pages.ts`, `LEGAL_PATHS` in `site-paths.ts`) and is imported. Don't type `href="/…"` for our own pages. Each page sets a title (`PAGE_TITLES`). A new address also goes in `netlify.toml`, the dev server and the reserved smart-link names.

## Before calling it done
- Run `npm run dev` and sign in with `/dev-login`. Look at the page and any pop-up it opens. Run `npm test`.
- Don't commit or deploy until the artist has seen it locally and said yes.
